/**
# Collections

Gad's composite types are **arrays** (ordered lists) and **dicts** (string-keyed
maps). Comprehensions live in [comprehensions.gad](comprehensions.gad),
keyValue arrays in [key_value_array.gad](key_value_array.gad), the
`map`/`filter`/`reduce` helpers in [functional.gad](functional.gad), and
destructuring in [destructuring.gad](destructuring.gad).

## Arrays

Indexable and mutable; `len` reports the length, `+=` concatenates, and slicing
returns a sub-array (negative indices count from the end). Their type, `array`,
is the array type of `any` items: `array === type []any` (see
[sized arrays](sized_arrays.gad#array-is-type-any)).

@snippet arrays

### `end`: the last index

Inside the brackets of an index or a slice, `end` is the **last index** of what
is indexed, as in Julia: `len(x) - 1` (gad counts from 0). `a[end]` is the last
item, `a[end-k]` the k-th before it, and it works in slices (`a[1:end]` — the
high bound excluded, as always —, `a[end-1:]`) and assignments
(`a[end] = v`, `a[end] += v`). What is indexed is evaluated once; the innermost
brackets own `end` (in `a[b[end]]` it is b's). Outside brackets `end` closes a
`begin … end` block, as before.

@snippet index_end

## Dicts

A dict maps string keys to values (items separated by commas or newlines). Read
with `.name` or `["name"]`, add/remove keys, and iterate key/value pairs. Nested
dicts may use block-style nesting (the outer parentheses are required because a
bare `{` at statement position starts a block).

@snippet dicts

### Keyword keys

A keyword (`class`, `if`, `else`, `func`, `false`, `nil`, …) may be used as a
**bare name** in any key position — it is taken as the string of its spelling.
This holds for `.name`, a dict key, `[name=value]` and `(;name=value)`, and for
the **names of members**: a field of an [interface](interfaces.gad) or a class,
a member, a key of a [contract](contracts.gad)'s `meta { … }` (`if? any`) — a
body item is never a statement there. Only the name position is affected; on
the value side keywords keep their meaning.

@snippet keyword_keys

### Concurrent dicts

`syncDict(d)` wraps a dict for concurrent use (reads and writes are
synchronized, for hosts that share it across goroutines); it reads and writes
like a dict, and `isSyncDict` tells it apart (it is not a plain `dict`).

@snippet sync_dict

## Spread and merge literals

`*expr` inside an array literal splices its elements in place (a leading spread
makes a fresh copy); inside a dict literal it merges another dict's entries, with
later entries winning.

@snippet spread

## Iteration

`for … in` yields (index, value) for arrays and (key, value) for dicts.

@snippet iterate
**/

//snippet arrays
a := [1, 2, 3]
a[1] = 20      // mutate in place
a = a + [4, 5] // concatenate (`a += x` appends x as a single element)
[a, len(a), a[0], a[-1], a[1:3], a[:-1]]
/**= [[1, 20, 3, 4, 5], 5, 1, 5, [20, 3], [1, 20, 3, 4]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet dicts
m := {a: 1, "b": 2, c: 3}
m.d = 4     // add a key
delete m.a  // remove a key (delete is a statement)
config := ({
    server {
        host: "localhost"
        port: 8080
    }
})
[m.b, m["d"], config.server.port]
/**= [2, 4, 8080] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet index_end
xs := [10, 20, 30, 40]
k := 2
ys := [1, 2, 3]
ys[end] = 30     // assign the last
ys[end-1] += 20
[xs[end], xs[end-1], xs[end-k], xs[1:end], xs[end-1:], xs[[0, 3][end]], ys]
/**= [40, 30, 20, [20, 30], [30, 40], 40, [1, 22, 30]] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet keyword_keys
mk := {class: 1, else: 2, func: 3} // keywords as bare string keys
interface Rule { if? str; for? int } // keywords as field names
r := {if: "x > 1", for: 2} :> Rule
[mk.class, mk["else"], mk.func, r.if, r.for]    // read via selector and index
/**= [1, 2, 3, "x > 1", 2] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet spread
sa := [1, 2]
sb := [3, 4]
arr := [0, *sa, *sb, 5]              // splice
dd := {a: 1, *{a: 9, b: 2}, c: 3}    // merge (later wins)
[arr, dd]
/**= [[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], {a: 9, b: 2, c: 3}] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet iterate
nums := [10, 20, 30]
squares := []
for _, n in nums { // arrays: (index, value)
    squares += n * n
}
person := {name: "Ada", age: 36}
for k, v in person { // dicts: (key, value)
    println(#"  {k} -> {v}")
}
squares
/**= [100, 400, 900] **/
//endsnippet

//snippet sync_dict
shared := syncDict({hits: 1})
shared.hits += 1
shared.users = ["ann"]
[shared.hits, shared.users, isSyncDict(shared), isDict(shared), typeName(shared)]
/**= [2, ["ann"], true, false, "syncDict"] **/
//endsnippet

return [1, 20, 3, 4, 5]
